# Configuration Guide

This project is for research/backtesting, not live trading.

```text
.env            backtest dates, image tag, and simulated capital
qkt.config.yaml data source and backtest runtime settings
data/           local market data mounted into the QKT container
strategies/     strategy files to test
```

## .env

Edit the research window and simulated starting capital:

```dotenv
QKT_IMAGE_TAG=v{{QKT_VERSION}}
BACKTEST_FROM=2024-01-01
BACKTEST_TO=2024-02-01
QKT_STARTING_BALANCE=10000
```

`BACKTEST_FROM` and `BACKTEST_TO` choose the dates. `QKT_STARTING_BALANCE` is
only simulated capital for the run.

## qkt.config.yaml

The generated config uses local market data from `/data`, which is mounted from
the project `data/` folder. If QKT cannot find data for the requested date or
symbol, the backtest cannot prove anything useful.

## Data

Put market data under `data/` in the format expected by QKT. Keep raw data and
generated reports separate so you can reproduce a run later.

## Strategy Files

`strategies/backtest.qkt` is the sample strategy. Replace or edit it, then run:

```bash
make backtest
```

